'''that''' (ᴛ̵ʜat), ''pron.'' or ''a.''; pl. ''those'' dial. ''thet''; < ME. ''that'', ''thet'', < AS. = OS. ''that'' = OFries. ''thet'', ''dat'' = MLG. ''dat'', that, = OHG. MH = Icel. ''that'', the, = Dan. ''det'', t this, = Goth. ''thata'', the; neut. c pron. which came to be used a AS. masc. ''se'', fem. ''seó'', neut. mod. E. in all genders, ''the'': see ''the''<sup>1</sup>. Hence ''that'', ''conj.'' and ''adv.'' ''pron.'' or ''a.'' 1. Used as a defin before a noun, in various sense {{smaller|a person or thing present or as before posed to be understood, or used to d thing or person emphatically, having n definite article ''the'', which may, howeve substituted for it.}}

{{smaller block|It shall be more tolerable for Sodom the day of judgment than for ''that'' city.}}

