as the substitute for an adjective: as, you allege that the man is ''innocent''; ''that'' he is not. Similarly, it is often used to introduce an explanation of something going before: as, "religion consists in living up to those principles—''that'' is, in acting in conformity to them." (''d'') Emphatically, in phrases expressive of approbation, applause, or encouragement.

